def H(code, d, q, right, wrong, e): return B.hand(code, d, q, right, wrong, e)

# ---- 746 Principles of Law, Public Safety, Corrections, and Security ----
H("746.d.1.A",3,"A cadet writes a clear incident summary using correct spelling, grammar and complete sentences. This applies:","English language arts skills needed in public safety careers",["only math skills","only artistic skills","no particular skills"],"Reports depend on strong writing.")
H("746.d.1.A",4,"Why do academy instructors grade cadets' written reports for grammar and organization?","Reports may be used as legal records and must be clear",["Grammar is only a hobby","Reports are never read","Spelling does not matter in court"],"Written reports can become evidence.")
H("746.d.1.B",3,"A dispatcher calculates how many minutes a unit needs to travel 12 miles at 36 miles per hour. This applies:","mathematics skills used in public safety careers",["art skills","music skills","no skills"],"12 ÷ 36 hour = 20 minutes.")
H("746.d.1.B",4,"A patrol unit covers 45 miles in 1.5 hours. Its average speed is:","30 miles per hour",["45 miles per hour","67.5 miles per hour","15 miles per hour"],"45 ÷ 1.5 = 30.")
H("746.d.1.C",3,"A crime-scene technician learns why fingerprints are unique to each person. This applies:","science knowledge used in law and public safety careers",["only cooking skills","only drawing skills","no science"],"Forensics relies on biology and chemistry.")
H("746.d.1.C",4,"Which science concept helps a fire investigator explain why a fire spread quickly in a room full of dry paper?","Fuel type and heat transfer affect how fast a fire grows",["Gravity stops fires","Paper cannot burn","Fires ignore materials"],"Combustion science explains fire behavior.")
H("746.d.2.A",3,"A new officer says 'me and him was there' in a briefing. A better evaluation of grammar would be to say:","'He and I were there'",["'Him and me was there'","'Me and him were there'","'He and me was there'"],"Standard grammar helps professional communication.")
H("746.d.2.A",4,"Why does correct grammar matter in verbal communication for public safety workers?","It makes instructions clear and keeps the speaker credible",["It makes talk slower only","It has no effect on listeners","It is only for writers"],"Clear speech prevents misunderstandings.")
H("746.d.2.B",3,"A firefighter gives short, firm commands to a crowd near a blaze but speaks gently to a frightened child. This shows:","choosing different speaking strategies for different audiences",["using one tone only","ignoring listeners","avoiding communication"],"Speaking style should fit the situation.")
H("746.d.2.B",4,"Which strategy best fits informing a large crowd about an evacuation?","Speak loudly, clearly and give short step-by-step directions",["Whisper long explanations","Use slang and jokes","Speak only to one person"],"Crowds need short clear commands.")
H("746.d.2.C",3,"A caller's trembling voice and fast speech tell a 911 operator the caller is frightened. This is an example of interpreting:","voice quality and delivery",["written grammar","uniform color","badge number"],"Tone and pace carry information.")
H("746.d.2.C",4,"A calm, steady, low voice used with an upset person is most likely to:","help de-escalate the situation",["increase panic","end the conversation","hide the message"],"Calm delivery reduces tension.")
H("746.d.2.D",3,"A police dispatcher and an EMT cooperate politely during a shared call. This demonstrates:","interpersonal skills needed to work with coworkers",["poor teamwork","avoidance","workplace conflict"],"Respect and cooperation help teams.")
H("746.d.2.D",4,"A coworker misunderstands your instructions during a shift. The best interpersonal response is to:","restate the instructions calmly and check understanding",["shout","ignore them","blame them publicly"],"Clarity and respect resolve confusion.")
H("746.d.3.A",3,"A security supervisor studies repeated after-hours alarms and proposes adding cameras. This is:","using analytical skills to form a proposal",["guessing","ignoring data","avoiding the problem"],"Analysis supports proposals.")
H("746.d.3.A",4,"Which step best supports a proposal to change patrol routes?","Reviewing incident data to find where problems occur most",["Choosing routes by coin toss","Copying another city exactly","Ignoring reports"],"Data should drive solutions.")
H("746.d.3.B",3,"A sheriff's office designs a plan so that rural residents can reach a deputy faster. This is:","formulating a solution that ensures delivery of services",["reducing service","ending service","hiding service"],"Service plans aim to reach people.")
H("746.d.3.B",4,"A proposal to improve 911 response times should explain:","what will change and how it will help residents",["only the logo","only past mistakes","nothing"],"Good proposals show benefit.")
H("746.d.3.C",3,"A correctional officer is asked to look away from a rule violation by a friend. Using critical thinking, the officer should:","weigh the ethics and follow the rules and policy",["ignore the policy","hide the violation","let the friend decide"],"Ethical issues require principled decisions.")
H("746.d.3.C",4,"A guard sees a coworker accept a gift from an inmate's family. Critical thinking about the ethical problem leads to:","reporting the violation through proper channels",["ignoring it","joining in","deleting records"],"Policy requires reporting.")
H("746.d.4.A",3,"Comparing the risks faced by a firefighter, a patrol officer and a corrections officer is an example of:","identifying and analyzing dangers in different career fields",["ignoring risks","avoiding safety","choosing jobs randomly"],"Each field has distinct hazards.")
H("746.d.4.A",4,"Which danger is most closely tied to firefighting?","Exposure to smoke, heat and structural collapse",["Paper cuts only","Eye strain only","Lack of air conditioning only"],"Fire scenes include heat, smoke and collapse.")
H("746.d.4.B",3,"After several back injuries, a department recommends lifting training and better equipment. This is:","creating strategies for employee safety and health",["ignoring injuries","punishing victims","removing safety rules"],"Strategies prevent repeat injuries.")
H("746.d.4.B",4,"A good strategy to reduce injuries at an emergency scene is to:","provide training and require protective equipment",["skip training","remove helmets","work faster without checks"],"Training and PPE protect workers.")
H("746.d.4.C",3,"Chemicals in a damaged truck leak near a roadway. Responders should:","follow hazardous materials handling procedures",["touch the liquid","ignore the spill","drive through it"],"Hazmat requires special handling.")
H("746.d.4.C",4,"Safety Data Sheets help responders by listing a chemical's:","hazards and safe handling and first aid information",["price","color of the label","delivery date"],"SDS describe hazards and precautions.")
H("746.d.4.D",3,"A fire academy requires regular workouts because good health and fitness help firefighters:","perform physically demanding duties safely",["avoid all training","skip rest","avoid teamwork"],"Fitness supports job performance.")
H("746.d.4.D",4,"Which habit best supports long-term fitness for a public safety worker?","Regular exercise, sleep and balanced eating",["Skipping sleep","Eating only snacks","Avoiding all exercise"],"Healthy habits sustain readiness.")
H("746.d.4.E",3,"A responder finds an adult who is not breathing and has no pulse. The responder should begin CPR and:","use an automated external defibrillator if one is available",["leave the scene","wait without acting","give water"],"CPR plus AED can restart a heart.")
H("746.d.4.E",4,"The purpose of an AED on a person in cardiac arrest is to:","analyze the heart rhythm and deliver a shock if needed",["measure height","take blood pressure","lower temperature"],"AEDs can restore a normal rhythm.")
H("746.d.5.A",3,"A trainee discusses whether an officer should keep a found wallet. This examination of an ethical dilemma focuses on:","professional conduct and honesty",["speed only","clothing only","weather only"],"Ethics guide conduct.")
H("746.d.5.A",4,"Which choice shows professional conduct for a guard who notices a coworker sleeping on duty?","Follow policy and report the problem appropriately",["Join in","Hide it forever","Post it online"],"Professionals follow policy.")
H("746.d.5.B",3,"An officer must obey search-and-seizure rules set by the Fourth Amendment and department policy. These are examples of:","laws, regulations and policies governing professionals",["suggestions only","jokes","myths"],"Professionals are bound by law and policy.")
H("746.d.5.B",4,"A department policy tells officers how and when force may be used. This type of rule is:","a policy that governs professional behavior",["a random opinion","optional advice","a game rule"],"Policies guide lawful conduct.")
H("746.d.5.C",3,"A supervisor asks a security guard to falsify a log. The best strategy is to:","refuse and report the request through proper channels",["comply quietly","delete the log","ignore the problem"],"Unethical orders must be reported.")
H("746.d.5.C",4,"An officer learns a coworker is stealing evidence. Which response recommends the right strategy?","Report it to a supervisor or internal affairs",["Take a share","Hide the evidence","Warn the coworker"],"Illegal acts must be reported.")
H("746.d.6.A",3,"After a major accident, police, fire, EMS and the court system each play a role. Discussing their importance shows how:","public safety agencies depend on one another",["agencies never meet","each works alone","only police matter"],"Agencies work together.")
H("746.d.6.A",4,"Which statement best explains why the court and corrections systems matter to public safety?","They hold offenders accountable and keep the community safe",["They only handle paperwork","They replace police","They end all crime"],"They complete the justice process.")
H("746.d.6.B",3,"The first person to arrive at a car crash checks for danger, calls for help and gives basic aid. This is a typical:","first responder role and responsibility",["spectator role","reporter role","tourist role"],"First responders provide immediate care.")
H("746.d.6.B",4,"Which is a first responder's responsibility at the scene of an emergency?","Make the scene safe and give immediate aid until others arrive",["Leave for lunch","Ignore injuries","Block help"],"Safety and aid come first.")
H("746.d.6.C",3,"A highway crash happens on the border of two counties, and both sheriff's offices argue over who should lead. This is a:","jurisdictional problem",["weather problem","dress code problem","staffing holiday"],"Jurisdiction is who has authority.")
H("746.d.6.C",4,"A good way to reduce jurisdictional confusion at a multi-agency scene is to:","use a clear command structure and shared communication",["let each agency act alone","stop communicating","ignore the boundary"],"Clear command prevents conflict.")
H("746.d.6.D",3,"A mall security guard can ask a rowdy visitor to leave private property, while a police officer can make an arrest under public authority. This shows that the roles:","differ between private security and public law enforcement",["are identical","never overlap with laws","have no limits"],"Authority differs.")
H("746.d.6.D",4,"Which task is usually done by a police officer but not by a typical private guard?","Making arrests under the authority of the government",["Watching a door","Checking visitor badges","Walking a patrol route"],"Police hold public arrest powers.")
H("746.d.7.A",3,"Laws in the United States come from the Constitution, statutes, court decisions and regulations. These are:","sources of law",["rumors","sports rules","advertising"],"Law has several sources.")
H("746.d.7.A",4,"Which is a source of law created by legislatures?","statutes",["myths","jokes","traditions of one family"],"Legislatures write statutes.")
H("746.d.7.B",3,"The Fourth Amendment protects people from unreasonable searches. This shows the Constitution's impact on:","how criminal law is enforced",["weather reports","school lunches","sports scores"],"Constitutional limits shape policing.")
H("746.d.7.B",4,"The Sixth Amendment gives an accused person the right to:","a speedy public trial and a lawyer",["avoid all charges","choose the judge's salary","skip court forever"],"Trial rights come from the Bill of Rights.")
H("746.d.7.C",3,"Theft of a candy bar is usually a misdemeanor, while armed robbery is a felony. The difference is mostly:","how serious the crime and punishment are",["the weather","the color of the weapon","the day of the week"],"Felonies are more serious.")
H("746.d.7.C",4,"Which punishment is generally linked to a felony conviction?","imprisonment for more than one year",["a library fine","a parking sticker","a verbal chat only"],"Felonies carry heavier penalties.")
H("746.d.7.D",3,"To convict someone of burglary, the state must prove each essential element, such as unlawful entry and intent. This is:","analyzing the elements of a crime",["guessing","ignoring facts","skipping evidence"],"All elements must be proved.")
H("746.d.7.D",4,"The elements of a crime generally include the criminal act and:","a guilty mental state when required",["a lucky outcome","a witness's age only","a uniform"],"Act and intent are common elements.")
H("746.d.7.E",3,"Officers sometimes struggle to prove a case when witnesses will not testify. This is a:","problem commonly associated with enforcing criminal laws",["perfect system","law-free zone","guaranteed win"],"Evidence and cooperation can be hard to secure.")
H("746.d.7.E",4,"Which problem often complicates enforcing criminal laws?","limited resources and difficulty gathering reliable evidence",["too many holidays","uniform colors","friendly neighbors"],"Resources and evidence limit enforcement.")
H("746.d.7.F",3,"A bill passes the House and Senate and is signed by the governor. This shows:","how a law is enacted",["how a trial works","how a jail runs","how a patrol is planned"],"Legislatures pass and executives sign bills.")
H("746.d.7.F",4,"Before a bill becomes a state law in Texas, it must be passed by both chambers and then:","signed by the governor or become law without a veto",["approved by the weather","burned","tried in court"],"The governor signs or allows it.")
H("746.d.8.A",3,"A student can become a city police officer, a county deputy, a state trooper or a federal agent. This lists:","career opportunities in law enforcement",["school rules","cooking jobs","sports teams"],"Careers exist at all levels.")
H("746.d.8.A",4,"Which agency would employ a Texas state trooper?","Texas Department of Public Safety",["a city library","a private mall","a school cafeteria"],"Troopers work for the DPS.")
H("746.d.8.B",3,"To become a Texas peace officer, a person must usually finish an academy and pass a licensing exam. This identifies:","required education and training for law enforcement",["no training","only a haircut","a membership card"],"Licensing requires training.")
H("746.d.8.B",4,"Compared with a local officer, a federal agent usually needs:","a college degree and specialized agency training",["no education","only a hobby","only a uniform"],"Federal roles have higher requirements.")
H("746.d.8.C",3,"Early American policing began with night watchmen and sheriffs before modern police departments formed. This is part of the:","history of policing in the United States",["history of cooking","history of music","history of sports"],"Policing evolved over time.")
H("746.d.8.C",4,"The first modern-style municipal police departments in the U.S. appeared mostly during the:","1800s in large cities",["1500s in forests","2000s in space","1700s in ships"],"Large cities created police forces in the 1800s.")
H("746.d.8.D",3,"Patrolling, answering calls and writing reports are all:","roles and responsibilities of law enforcement professionals",["unrelated tasks","hobbies","entertainment"],"These are core duties.")
H("746.d.8.D",4,"An officer's responsibility to enforce laws fairly means the officer must:","treat people equally and follow the law",["pick favorites","skip procedures","ignore rights"],"Fair enforcement is required.")
H("746.d.8.E",3,"Rules about when an officer may arrest someone or use force come from constitutional law. This is the:","impact of constitutional law on police actions",["effect of weather","effect of fashion","effect of snacks"],"Constitutional limits shape police power.")
H("746.d.8.E",4,"Which standard must usually be met before an officer can make an arrest?","probable cause",["a hunch only","a rumor","a coin flip"],"Arrests require probable cause.")
H("746.d.8.F",3,"Paramedics treat injured people on-scene and transport them to a hospital. This shows the role of:","emergency medical services in public safety",["court clerks","jail cooks","traffic signs"],"EMS provides emergency care.")
H("746.d.8.F",4,"EMS contributes to public safety by:","giving rapid medical care and transport during emergencies",["writing tickets","building roads","grading papers"],"EMS saves lives.")
H("746.d.8.G",3,"After a difficult call, a dispatcher talks with a peer support team and takes a walk. This is:","managing the stress of public safety work",["avoiding recovery","ignoring needs","hiding feelings forever"],"Healthy coping reduces stress.")
H("746.d.8.G",4,"Which habit helps public safety professionals manage job-related stress?","Exercise, rest and talking with trusted peers or counselors",["Skipping sleep","Isolating","Refusing help"],"Support and healthy habits help.")
H("746.d.9.A",3,"A student could work as a court clerk, bailiff or probation officer. This identifies:","career opportunities in the court systems",["only police jobs","only teaching jobs","only kitchen jobs"],"Courts employ many roles.")
H("746.d.9.A",4,"Which job helps keep order and security in a courtroom?","bailiff",["cook","pilot","painter"],"Bailiffs maintain courtroom order.")
H("746.d.9.B",3,"A city municipal court handles minor offenses, while a district court handles more serious cases. This identifies:","levels and functions of criminal courts",["school grades","bus routes","recipes"],"Courts differ by level.")
H("746.d.9.B",4,"A court that reviews whether a trial court made a legal error is a:","court of appeals",["traffic light","jury","city council"],"Appeals courts review legal error.")
H("746.d.9.C",3,"The judge, prosecutor and defense attorney are part of the:","courtroom work group",["audience only","jury only","police squad"],"They work together in the court process.")
H("746.d.9.C",4,"Which member of the courtroom work group presents the state's case against the accused?","the prosecutor",["the bailiff","the defendant","the juror"],"Prosecutors represent the government.")
H("746.d.9.D",3,"Before trial, the accused appears at an arraignment to hear the charges and enter a plea. This is an example of:","pretrial procedures",["post-trial appeals","sentencing","parole review"],"Arraignment is pretrial.")
H("746.d.9.D",4,"During a trial, jurors are asked to decide:","whether the evidence proves guilt beyond a reasonable doubt",["what time court ends","who pays the judge","the weather"],"The standard is beyond a reasonable doubt.")
H("746.d.9.E",3,"A judge orders probation instead of prison for a first-time offender. This is a type of:","sentencing",["arrest","booking","bail"],"Probation is a sentence.")
H("746.d.9.E",4,"A sentence that allows an offender to remain in the community under supervision is:","probation",["a pardon","an acquittal","an arraignment"],"Probation allows supervised release.")
H("746.d.10.A",3,"A student could become a probation officer, parole officer or correctional officer. This explains:","career opportunities in the correctional system",["only banking careers","only farm careers","only film careers"],"Corrections includes several careers.")
H("746.d.10.A",4,"A professional who supervises offenders released from prison before their sentence ends is a:","parole officer",["bailiff","court reporter","dispatcher"],"Parole officers supervise releases.")
H("746.d.10.B",3,"Supervising inmates, enforcing rules and keeping order are:","duties of a correctional officer",["hobbies","courtroom duties","fire duties"],"These are core duties.")
H("746.d.10.B",4,"A correctional officer must watch inmates, keep the facility secure and:","write accurate reports about incidents",["avoid documentation","ignore rules","leave the post"],"Reports are required.")
H("746.d.10.C",3,"Early American prisons, such as those that used solitary reflection, were created to:","punish offenders and encourage reform",["feed tourists","entertain crowds","train astronauts"],"Early prisons aimed at reform.")
H("746.d.10.C",4,"The idea of a penitentiary was based on the belief that offenders could:","reflect and reform through isolation and labor",["never change","avoid punishment","earn trophies"],"Penitentiaries emphasized reform.")
H("746.d.10.D",3,"A person arrested Friday is held for a few days in the county facility awaiting a hearing, while a convicted felon serves years elsewhere. The first place is a jail and the second is a:","prison",["library","hospital","court"],"Jails hold short-term; prisons hold long-term.")
H("746.d.10.D",4,"Which best distinguishes a jail from a prison?","Jails hold people awaiting trial or serving short sentences",["Jails are only for felons with long sentences","Jails are for juveniles only","They are identical"],"Jails are short-term.")
H("746.d.10.E",3,"A facility labeled minimum, medium or maximum security reflects:","levels of security in prisons and jails",["school grade levels","ticket prices","classroom sizes"],"Facilities are classified by security level.")
H("746.d.10.E",4,"Which type of facility houses inmates who pose the highest risk?","maximum security",["minimum security","a visitor center","an arraignment hall"],"Maximum security is the strictest.")
H("746.d.10.F",3,"Inmates still keep certain protections, such as freedom from cruel and unusual punishment. These are:","constitutional rights of inmates",["no rights","only rumors","privileges of staff"],"The Eighth Amendment still applies.")
H("746.d.10.F",4,"The Eighth Amendment protects inmates from:","cruel and unusual punishment",["all supervision","all rules","all meals"],"Inmates keep this protection.")
H("746.d.11.A",3,"A person could be a security guard, a loss-prevention agent or a private investigator. This explains:","career opportunities in private security",["only court careers","only fire careers","only teaching careers"],"Private security has many roles.")
H("746.d.11.A",4,"Which job is typically found in private security?","retail loss-prevention officer",["state trooper","judge","county sheriff"],"Retail stores use loss-prevention staff.")
H("746.d.11.B",3,"Private security grew in the United States as businesses and railroads hired guards to protect property. This is part of the:","history and importance of private security",["history of cooking","history of music","history of toys"],"Business needs drove its growth.")
H("746.d.11.B",4,"Private security is important to society because it:","protects people and property that public agencies cannot always cover",["replaces all police","ends crime","has no laws"],"It supplements public safety.")
H("746.d.11.C",3,"A mall guard calls the police after catching a thief and gives a statement. This shows the:","relationship between private security and public safety agencies",["rivalry only","no connection","identical authority"],"The two cooperate.")
H("746.d.11.C",4,"Private security most often helps public police by:","reporting crimes and sharing information",["making arrests in every city","ignoring crimes","blocking investigations"],"They share information.")
H("746.d.12.A",3,"Becoming a firefighter, arson investigator or fire inspector are examples of:","career opportunities in fire protection services",["court careers","cooking careers","sports careers"],"Fire services have many roles.")
H("746.d.12.A",4,"A professional who examines buildings for fire-code violations is a:","fire inspector",["bailiff","parole officer","dispatcher"],"Inspectors enforce fire codes.")
H("746.d.12.B",3,"Fighting fires, rescuing people and giving emergency medical aid are:","duties and responsibilities of firefighters",["court duties","school duties","bank duties"],"These are core firefighter duties.")
H("746.d.12.B",4,"A firefighter's responsibilities go beyond fires to include:","medical aid and rescue calls",["only parades","only paperwork","only driving trucks for fun"],"Many calls are medical.")
H("746.d.12.C",3,"A 911 call-taker enters an address in a computer-aided dispatch system so the nearest unit is sent. This shows the importance of:","911 operations and computer-aided dispatch",["paper maps only","guessing","ignoring calls"],"CAD speeds the response.")
H("746.d.12.C",4,"Computer-aided dispatch helps responders by:","tracking calls and units to send the closest help quickly",["slowing calls","hiding units","deleting records"],"CAD coordinates resources.")
H("746.d.12.D",3,"A house fire with an injured resident requires police to control traffic, firefighters to fight the fire and EMS to treat the victim. This shows the:","relationships among police, fire and emergency medical services",["lack of cooperation","single agency work","no teamwork"],"Agencies coordinate at scenes.")
H("746.d.12.D",4,"Why do police, fire and EMS train together?","to coordinate during joint emergency responses",["to compete","to avoid contact","to switch jobs"],"Joint training improves coordination.")
H("746.d.13.A",3,"A student joins a career and technical student organization such as SkillsUSA and a law enforcement explorer post. This is:","participating in community and career organizations",["avoiding involvement","quitting school","ignoring careers"],"Organizations build skills.")
H("746.d.13.A",4,"A benefit of joining an organization like SkillsUSA is:","building leadership and career skills",["avoiding teamwork","ending training","losing opportunities"],"They support career readiness.")
H("746.d.13.B",3,"Neighbors form a Citizens on Patrol group to watch for suspicious activity and report it. This is a:","community outreach organization",["private army","school club for sports only","tax office"],"Citizens on Patrol assist police.")
H("746.d.13.B",4,"Community outreach programs like neighborhood watch help public safety by:","building trust and reporting concerns to authorities",["replacing police","ending laws","hiding crimes"],"Partnership improves safety.")

B.balance()
